// What the `dotnet` command is told when it is run in this folder or below it. It
// looks for a file of this name in the folder it is run in and then in each folder
// above, which is why the Windows app is built and tested from here:
//
//     cd windows
//     dotnet test
//
// ONE THING IS SAID: how tests are run. `dotnet test` has two ways. The old one
// (VSTest) is what it does unless told otherwise. The tests here are xUnit's third
// version, which from its 4.0 runs on the new one (Microsoft.Testing.Platform), and
// from the .NET 10 SDK on the old way refuses such tests outright. Without this file,
// or run from the top of the repository, `dotnet test` stops with "Testing with VSTest
// target is no longer supported".
//
// ONE THING IS NOT SAID, on purpose: which version of the SDK. Any from .NET 10 on
// builds these projects. Naming .NET 10's alone would stop the build on the day Visual
// Studio replaced that SDK with the next.
{
  "test": {
    "runner": "Microsoft.Testing.Platform"
  }
}
